INSTRUCTION 0007 | 0xa | 48 81 ec 38 01 00 00 | sub    rsp,0x138
  Section or entry point: dqrdc2_.
  Long operation: Subtract fixed-width integers and update arithmetic condition flags.
  Detailed first-pass effect: Read current rsp and 0x138; subtract source from destination at the destination's encoded integer width and store the low-width result in rsp; set the defined carry, overflow, sign, zero, parity and auxiliary flags (subject to exact width and operands).
  Sequential successor if not otherwise redirected or faulting: 0x11 (7 bytes).
  Link-time relocation: none.

INSTRUCTION 0008 | 0x11 | 48 63 36 | movsxd rsi,DWORD PTR [rsi]
  Section or entry point: dqrdc2_.
  Long operation: Extend a signed four-byte integer into an eight-byte register.
  Detailed first-pass effect: Read a signed 32-bit integer from DWORD PTR [rsi], copy its sign into the high bits, and write the 64-bit result to rsi; do not change arithmetic flags.
  Sequential successor if not otherwise redirected or faulting: 0x14 (3 bytes).
  Link-time relocation: none.

