  Detailed first-pass effect: Read DWORD PTR [rcx] at the width indicated by this encoding and write the resulting bit pattern to r11d. If this writes a 32-bit general register, its encompassing 64-bit register has its upper 32 bits cleared. A memory read/write is observable; condition flags do not change.
